        "code": "# Who secures what? \"you\" = the customer, \"provider\" = AWS / Azure / GCP\nLAYERS = [\n    \"data\", \"identities\", \"application\", \"runtime\",\n    \"operating system\", \"virtualization\", \"physical datacenter\",\n]\n\n# Index of the first layer managed by the provider, for each service model\nFIRST_PROVIDER_LAYER = {\"on-prem\": 7, \"iaas\": 5, \"paas\": 3, \"saas\": 2}\n\n\ndef owner(model, layer):\n    return \"provider\" if LAYERS.index(layer) >= FIRST_PROVIDER_LAYER[model] else \"you\"\n\n\nprint(f\"{'layer':<20}{'on-prem':<10}{'iaas':<10}{'paas':<10}saas\")\nfor layer in LAYERS:\n    row = \"\".join(f\"{owner(m, layer):<10}\" for m in FIRST_PROVIDER_LAYER)\n    print(f\"{layer:<20}{row}\".rstrip())\n\n# Data and identities never move to the provider column\nalways_yours = [l for l in LAYERS if all(owner(m, l) == \"you\" for m in FIRST_PROVIDER_LAYER)]\nprint(\"\\nAlways your job:\", \", \".join(always_yours))\n",
